       Take the parameter by reference instead, so the recursive call reborrows to the SAME type and `S` is a fixed point:

           fn eval<S: ..>(arg: &mut S, ..)      // signature

           eval(&mut *arg, ..)                  // recursive call

       If the by-value signature is part of a public API, keep it as a provided entry point that delegates once to the by-reference method. Erasing the parameter behind one fixed type (`&mut dyn Trait`) also closes it, at the cost of virtual dispatch.
